# MAPPING_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md

> **Read this file first.** It is the cross-session source of truth for the deterministic
> DOCX <-> tagged-PDF math mapping work (Steps A-F). Assume zero prior context.
>
> **Scope guard (do not break):** the *comparison* stage (Step 3, image-based comparison of
> mapped math) was **not touched**. All new code is additive and opt-out-able; the mapping
> engine never rewrites `alignment_pairs` / `comparison_pairs`.
>
> Last updated: 2026-09-30 (tag-order + monotone-DP round).

## 0. TL;DR

* New deterministic mapping engine: `math_mapping.py` (Steps B-F) + `math_canonicalize.py`
  (Step A). No ML, no paid APIs, no network. Optional extras (`sympy`, `latex2sympy2`,
  `pylatexenc`, LaTeXML, sentence-transformers) are probed and degraded gracefully.
* New pytest harness: `tests/mapping_pair_harness.py` (library + CLI) driven by
  `tests/test_mapping_pairs.py`, with one JSON fixture per pair under
  `tests/fixtures/mapping_pairs/`. Adding a file pair = adding a test; there is **no**
  per-file code (and no `if filename == ...` anywhere).
* Integration is one additive call: `attach_mapping_engine_result(...)` at the end of
  `compare_raw_docx_to_tagged_pdf`, recording `mapping_engine` + diagnostics in the payload.
* Current harness result: **mean F1 = 0.8182 over 16 pairs, 8/16 at the 0.95 target**
  (same harness with legacy settings: mean F1 0.6941, 4/16). The mean is dragged down by a
  handful of content-less pairs (MathType DOCX vs placeholder-only PDF) whose *reference*
  alignment is itself only partly recoverable from the available signals - see §3.5.
  (Historical note: earlier notes quote a 0.632 baseline. That number came from the *older*
  harness/scoring conventions; since the harness and fixtures were reworked, the apples-to-
  apples comparison is 0.6941 -> 0.8182 on identical inputs, which is the delta this work
  delivers.)
* Key algorithmic finding of the last round: the reference alignments are (nearly) order
  preserving, and the PDF **tag order** is the order that mirrors DOCX authoring order;
  geometric reading order is now opt-in. See §1.6/§1.7.

