| experiment | result | decision |
|---|---|---|
| geometric reading order as default | worse on 9/15 pairs, 757 vs 1607 residual inversions; two pairs collapse (743: 1.000 -> 0.376, 1158: 1.000 -> 0.753) | rejected as default, kept as opt-in flag |
| single global monotone DP (no Step D regions) | mean F1 0.7990 vs engine 0.8061; 8948 0.587 vs 0.748, 12344 0.906 vs 0.862, 12483 0.663 vs 0.550 | rejected: region cutting is net positive (`temp/probe_global_dp.py`) |
| re-weighting for content-less pairs (`temp/probe_weight_variants.py`: drop `position`, drop `section`, label- or context-heavy) | all variants lose on the mean: base 0.7815, nopos 0.7135, nosection 0.7583, nopos_nosect 0.7245, label_heavy 0.7713, context_heavy 0.7332, nopos_label_ctx 0.7261 vs engine 0.8061. Individual wins (MEC_70463 0.824 with `nopos`, 12483 0.694 with `nopos_nosect`) trade against larger losses elsewhere | rejected as per-pair overfitting; no adaptive weighting implemented |
| lowering the accept floor to convert `partner_fn` into matches | rejected: those partners score below the floor precisely when label *and* context are weak; accepting them adds false positives that cost more precision than the recall they buy |
| Hungarian inside regions (`use_monotone_assignment=0`) | recovers the one non-monotone pair (12344 +0.004) but loses every monotone pair; mean -0.124 | kept only as fallback flag |
| per-file tuning / `if pair_id == ...` branches | not implemented | forbidden by the task |

### 3.7 Known limitations

1. The reference for each pair is the *legacy* pipeline's alignment (or, for pairs with no
   sidecar, the current engine's own output). It is not verified ground truth, and for 4 pairs
   it is provably non-order-preserving. Squeezing the last points out of those pairs means
   either reproducing the legacy quirks or getting a human to review the 16 fixtures
   (`status: VERIFIED`) - both are outside deterministic mapping.
2. Nothing here is tuned per document, so a genuinely new producer style (scrambled tag order,
   no prose context, no visible numbers, no math text) has no signal left to use. The
   `pdf_reading_order` / `monotone_assignment` / weight / threshold env keys exist so such a
   pair can be diagnosed without code changes.
3. `visual` and `embedding` components exist but are off (weight 0.0). Turning them on needs
   extra dependencies and would break the "free, offline, deterministic" promise for the
   default path, so it is deliberately not done.
4. Diagnostics are capped (see the score-matrix cap in `math_mapping.py`) to protect memory on
   pathological documents; above the cap the candidate CSV is skipped with a warning.


