## Round 16 — Cross-encoder reranker eval: NEGATIVE RESULT

Attempted: train MiniLM cross-encoder over the candidate dump (K=10 per docx
item), val on 599/544/12483, compare p@1 vs baseline match_score.

Result: baseline p@1 = 0.147, cross-encoder p@1 = 0.137 (delta -0.010).
Per-file: 544 down 0.076, 599 up 0.024, 12483 unchanged.

Verdict: cross-encoder does not beat baseline. Do NOT integrate.

Key takeaway: baseline p@1 on these three files is 0.15 — the current
matcher picks the wrong top candidate 85% of the time. This is a
segmentation/granularity/extraction problem, not a scoring problem.
Next investigation should target why the correct candidate is not being
ranked first, not how to score better.
